[center][size=6][color=#93c47d][b]CSS v1.0.2[/b][/color][/size][/center]

[b]Added[/b]
[list]
[*]Adjust Travel for supported body-motion rigs, with separate values for each supported body part.
[*]Support the expanded body-shape controls in Eve 1.5.1, Unholy Genessa 0.3.1 and Commander White 0.1.2. An optional UUEPBS profile exposes their 24 body morphs and chest bones.
[/list]

[b]Fixed[/b]
[list]
[*]Apply the motion travel shown by the active preset, including older saved looks that have no stored Travel value.
[*]Reduce redundant updates during facial-animation playback.
[*]Recognize Merrick replacement mods and refresh non-CSS character detection for the October 20 game update.
[*]Assign native ghost materials to William and Ball Boy's second look in Use NPC / Enemy.
[/list]

[b]CSS Shared Assets 1.0.2[/b]
[list]
[*]Keep shared animations and facial playback working with the updated outfit packages.
[*]The gray-texture repairs are included in each affected outfit's own update. Update those outfits as well as CSS and Shared Assets.
[/list]

[b]Upgrading[/b]
[list]
[*]Close the game and install CSS 1.0.2 plus CSS Shared Assets 1.0.2.
[*]Replace each affected outfit with its new full package. Keep the three container files together.
[*]Remove superseded standalone shader-fix overlays. Keep CustomShellSystem/state and your profiles.
[/list]

Motion-feel tuning and the Commander White frame-rate investigation continue; this update does not claim those reports are fully resolved.
